ins at 30.0 degrees for two consecutive thirty-minute windows; expanded activation begins at 32.0 degrees, so one 31.4-degree observation is insufficient for expansion.\nForecast probability of exceeding the expanded threshold is 0.62, while the observed station coverage is 84 percent. Probability and measurement coverage must not be exchanged or multiplied.\nA sensor relocation, calibration, forecast model, district boundary, or candidate operating-map change makes prior hazard evidence stale for the affected scope.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSHELTER and TRANSIT staging consume CLIMATE district triggers; COMMS may publish only the operating state authorized by COUNCIL.\nLINEAGE records map changes and REVIEW requires current candidate-bound threshold evidence.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CLI-000 | north-district | v3 | 39.0 | degrees-C-WBGT | superseded |\n| CLI-001 | river-district | v3 | 40.7 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-002 | central-core | v3 | 39.5 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-003 | hillside | v3 | 41.2 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-004 | north-district | v3 | 40.0 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-005 | river-district | v3 | 41.7 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-006 | central-core | v3 | 40.5 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-007 | hillside | v3 | 39.3 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-008 | north-district | v3 | 41.0 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-009 | river-district | v3 | 39.8 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-010 | central-core | v3 | 41.5 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-011 | hillside | v3 | 40.3 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-012 | north-district | v3 | 39.1 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-013 | river-district | v4 | 40.8 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-014 | central-core | v4 | 39.6 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-015 | hillside | v4 | 41.3 | degrees-C-WBGT | current |\n| CLI-016 | north-district |