\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Decision` and containing exactly these\n   ordered level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and operating states`\n   2. `Heat triggers and geographic staging`\n   3. `Power, water, and cooling continuity`\n   4. `Clinical, shelter, and accessibility operations`\n   5. `Transit, communications, logistics, and staffing`\n   6. `Execution, rollback, verification, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,200–1,650 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. Reconcile authority,\nhazard thresholds, power, water, clinical surge, cooling-center capacity,\naccessible transit, public communication, logistics, staffing, candidate\nlineage, and independent readiness.\n\nBind each action and gate to owners, prerequisites, observations, the current\ncandidate, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that retires temporary controls.\nPreserve observations versus gates, probability versus coverage, installed\nversus usable capacity, reserve versus flow, median versus percentile, hours\nversus days, source-local authority, and current versus stale evidence.\n\nChecks are candidate-bound mechanical feedback. They do not independently\nauthorize operations, readiness, submission, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-001 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:COUNCIL:1-60+CLIMATE:1-60\",\"object_version\":\"e316c261db70916999bfbfdb56ed0316408b03aeabcce976774ede78e612dd0e\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-001\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"COUNCIL\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"CLIMATE\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8207}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"COUNCIL\",\"source_path\":\"sources/COUNCIL_AUTHORITY.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"1dcfd09e66f004f0cf3b7849dcc7ca097d4d6135809649c33d6cb1784dac88ea\",\"source_size_bytes\":5794,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Heat emergency authority and public operating states\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nThe emergency manager may activate cooling operations and emergency procurement. Only the health commissioner may authorize a citywide heat-health emergency, and only the continuity director may close the incident after current infrastructure, clinical, shelter, transit, staffing, and audit evidence is reconciled.\nA successful mechanical check is not health authority or closure authority. Emergency procurement does not waive water-quality, accessibility, labor, privacy, evidence-custody, or independent-review obligations.\nA handoff is valid only when the receiver acknowledges the same operating map, facility roster, current demand model, communications release, and candidate version. Version mismatch blocks closure.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nCLIMATE supplies hazard thresholds, GRID and WATER supply infrastructure state, and REVIEW supplies independent findings; none may authorize closure.\nLINEAGE binds the current candidate while COUNCIL separates activation, limited operations, expanded operations, and closure.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| AUT-000 | incident-command | v3 | 1.0 | approval | superseded |\n| AUT-001 | health-office | v3 | 2.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-002 | utility-desk | v3 | 1.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-003 | public-liaison | v3 | 3.2 | approval | current |\n| AUT-004 | incident-command | v3 | 2.0 | approval | current |\n| AUT-005 | health-office | v3 | 3.7 | approval | current |\n| AUT-006 | utility-desk | v3 | 2.5 | approval | current |\n| AUT-007 | public-liaison | v3 | 1.3 | approval | current |\n| AUT-008 | incident-command | v3 | 3.0 | approval |