 `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Decision` and containing exactly these\n   ordered level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and operating states`\n   2. `Heat triggers and geographic staging`\n   3. `Power, water, and cooling continuity`\n   4. `Clinical, shelter, and accessibility operations`\n   5. `Transit, communications, logistics, and staffing`\n   6. `Execution, rollback, verification, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,200–1,650 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. Reconcile authority,\nhazard thresholds, power, water, clinical surge, cooling-center capacity,\naccessible transit, public communication, logistics, staffing, candidate\nlineage, and independent readiness.\n\nBind each action and gate to owners, prerequisites, observations, the current\ncandidate, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that retires temporary controls.\nPreserve observations versus gates, probability versus coverage, installed\nversus usable capacity, reserve versus flow, median versus percentile, hours\nversus days, source-local authority, and current versus stale evidence.\n\nChecks are candidate-bound mechanical feedback. They do not independently\nauthorize operations, readiness, submission, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-003 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:GRID:1-60+WATER:1-60\",\"object_version\":\"d1ecb3814186f1a6327e7fa1b8a7befd76b1617b06163bb6a426511c6e355be8\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-003\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"GRID\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"WATER\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":7344}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"GRID\",\"source_path\":\"sources/GRID_COOLING_POWER.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"2149dcb753ebd817f10869d394e30f61e89ac46d6d4de2ace9bde1cb7c13299d\",\"source_size_bytes\":5546,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Cooling power, feeder limits, and backup capacity\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nInstalled cooling-service capacity is 31.0 megawatts, while current usable capacity after feeder derating is 24.5 megawatts. Installed and usable capacity must not be added or swapped.\nFeeder voltage is 12.6 kilovolts and must remain between 12.2 and 12.9 kilovolts at every critical node for three consecutive fifteen-minute windows. A system average cannot replace every-node compliance.\nBackup generation supplies 8.4 megawatts for sixteen hours at emergency cooling load, but only nine hours at full public load. The load regimes and durations remain distinct.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nSHELTER occupancy and CLINIC surge demand depend on GRID; SUPPLY controls fuel duration and WATER depends on powered pumps.\nA feeder, transformer, relay, fuel stock, or facility-load change makes earlier power evidence stale.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| GRD-000 | feeder-east | v3 | 28.0 | megawatts | superseded |\n| GRD-001 | feeder-west | v3 | 29.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-002 | library-hub | v3 | 28.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-003 | backup-plant | v3 | 30.2 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-004 | feeder-east | v3 | 29.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-005 | feeder-west | v3 | 30.7 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-006 | library-hub | v3 | 29.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-007 | backup-plant | v3 | 28.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-008 | feeder-east | v3 | 30.0 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-009 | feeder-west | v3 | 28.8 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-010 | library-hub | v3 | 30.5 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-011 | backup-plant | v3 | 29.3 | megawatts | current |\n| GRD-012 | feeder-east | v3 | 28.1 | meg