y externalized source ID>\nSOURCE_VERSION: <exact 64-hex version>\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: <exact newly externalized RESULT ID>\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: <one exact unique single-line substring copied from that source inside the delivered result>\nMODE: source_reported_fact or source_reported_relationship\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE or comma-separated exact source IDs named by both the statement and the anchor's containing source line\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: <one complete single-line source-attributed fact or relationship>\n\nThe host, not you, resolves the exact anchor, derives its containing complete source line, byte offsets, hashes, source/version binding, and reopen path. Copy only the smallest exact substring that supports the statement. The containing line preserves adjacent context and qualifications. Each claim is admitted independently; rejected claims consume cost and are discarded without repair or retry. A zero-valid update leaves prior state unchanged and ordinary task work continues.\n\nEmit at most 4 claims per source and 8 total, <= 1500 tokenizer tokens overall and <= 650 per source. A fact cannot name an external source. A relationship may name external objects when the owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nGRID: 2149dcb753ebd817f10869d394e30f61e89ac46d6d4de2ace9bde1cb7c13299d\nWATER: 99ff010ef7c523ff6805b118fb7678a403caf6cfb047f9a7607832a51f1e4291\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\nNON-AUTHORITATIVE, INCOMPLETE SEMANTIC RESIDUE. Omission is not evidence that a source or requirement was covered. Exact sources remain reopenable.\n\n## CLAIM GRID-FINDING-BACKUP\nSLOT_SOURCE: GRID\nSOURCE_VERSION: 2149dcb753ebd817f10869d394e30f61e89ac46d6d4de2ace9bde1cb7c13299d\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-003\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Backup generation supplies 8.4 megawatts for sixteen hours at emergency cooling load, but only nine hours at full public load.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 463-589\nANCHOR_SHA256: 2e4f7133e72002eda64f35e10403e9702daae54f71b428742f4c5aba477c1027\nCONTEXT_LINES: 7-7\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 168ddf1fc281514d273a78ae1098c29be9d4f16fd3ebf689328b7edd1ef0dfcb\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: GRID reports backup generation supplies 8.4 megawatts for sixteen hours at emergency cooling load and nine hours at full public load.\n\n## CLAIM GRID-FINDING-CAPACITY\nSLOT_SOURCE: GRID\nSOURCE_VERSION: 2149dcb753ebd817f10869d394e30f61e89ac46d6d4de2ace9bde1cb7c13299d\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-003\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Installed cooling-service capacity is 31.0 megawatts, while current usable capacity after feeder derating is 24.5 megawatts.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 73-197\nANCHOR_SHA256: 0b0b5964943b61cd3a1d690ee7eec2943cb272fc1d824e7e58ab5433d7c02e42\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 58aa40bcf8857a7a78dc4c492d0d0ccd72ec5990d23e7b64e01650b94f7b7feb\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: GRID reports installed cooling-service capacity as 31.0 megawatts and current usable capacity after feeder derating as 24.5 megawatts.\n\n## CLAIM WATER-FINDING-PRESSURE\nSLOT_SOURCE: WATER\nSOURCE_VERSION: 99ff010ef7c523ff6805b118fb7678a403caf6cfb047f9a7607832a51f1e4291\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: RESULT-003\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: Public cooling sites require at least 35 psi at every served node for three consecutive ten-minute windows; one network average is insufficient.\nANCHOR_BYTES: 108-252\nANCHOR_SHA256: d016282341353e1546a3b48ef8265da2d747a692cb3a93a34bae3b3644a08575\nCONTEXT_LINES: 5-5\nCONTEXT_SHA256: 572d12d5532a0928a438cae936d9e04e4fb391577f6c2853805c426fcfc0a9ea\nMODE: source_reported_fact\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENT