ck, and resupply\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nGenerator fuel covers sixteen hours at emergency cooling load and nine hours at full public load. The two consumption regimes must remain distinct.\nBottled water covers 2.8 operating days, while cooling packs cover 3.6 clinic-days. Operating days and clinic-days are different inventory measures.\nThree potable tankers arrive at 18:20 UTC with uncertainty of plus or minus thirty-five minutes; planned arrival is not deployed capacity.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nGRID backup duration and WATER replenishment depend on SUPPLY; CLINIC and SHELTER consume different stocks.\nCLIMATE may alter delivery routes and LABOR must qualify receiving and distribution teams.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| SUP-000 | generator-fuel | v3 | 16.0 | hours-cover | superseded |\n| SUP-001 | bottled-water | v3 | 17.7 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-002 | cooling-packs | v3 | 16.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-003 | tanker-fleet | v3 | 18.2 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-004 | generator-fuel | v3 | 17.0 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-005 | bottled-water | v3 | 18.7 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-006 | cooling-packs | v3 | 17.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-007 | tanker-fleet | v3 | 16.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-008 | generator-fuel | v3 | 18.0 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-009 | bottled-water | v3 | 16.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-010 | cooling-packs | v3 | 18.5 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-011 | tanker-fleet | v3 | 17.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-012 | generator-fuel | v3 | 16.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-013 | bottled-water | v4 | 17.8 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-014 | cooling-packs | v4 | 16.6 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-015 | tanker-fleet | v4 | 18.3 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-016 | generator-fuel | v4 | 17.1 | hours-cover | current |\n| SUP-017 | bottled-water | v4 | 18.8 | hours-cover | curre