y externalized source ID>\nSOURCE_VERSION: <exact 64-hex version>\nEVIDENCE_RESULT: <exact newly externalized RESULT ID>\nEVIDENCE_ANCHOR: <one exact unique single-line substring copied from that source inside the delivered result>\nMODE: source_reported_fact or source_reported_relationship\nATTRIBUTION: owner_source_reported\nREFERENTS: NONE or comma-separated exact source IDs named by both the statement and the anchor's containing source line\nAUTHORITY: non_authoritative_derivative\nSTATEMENT: <one complete single-line source-attributed fact or relationship>\n\nThe host, not you, resolves the exact anchor, derives its containing complete source line, byte offsets, hashes, source/version binding, and reopen path. Copy only the smallest exact substring that supports the statement. The containing line preserves adjacent context and qualifications. Each claim is admitted independently; rejected claims consume cost and are discarded without repair or retry. A zero-valid update leaves prior state unchanged and ordinary task work continues.\n\nEmit at most 4 claims per source and 8 total, <= 1500 tokenizer tokens overall and <= 650 per source. A fact cannot name an external source. A relationship may name external objects when the owner-source context names them, but cannot mutate their slots or assert their authoritative current state. Cross-source synthesis belongs in exact task work, not this register.\n\nNEW SOURCE VERSIONS\nCLINIC: f8db85fe7f667c38151156fa2c5c25f3601462976e555f637ccff746c13a34b4\nSHELTER: dcd71253d29841bf14beafb1e65b01527aa9c8dab2d65d352537ea6faec725fb\n\nPRIOR CURRENT RECORDS FOR THESE SOURCES\n# Anchored provenance-local source register\n\nEMPTY\n\n\nAUTHORITATIVE TASK (relevance only; never evidence)\n# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Task\n\nProduce two exact, source-grounded work products for the synthetic Trellis\nurban heat emergency:\n\n1. `EVIDENCE_INTEGRATION_LEDGER.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Evidence-to-Requirement Matrix`.\n2. `BOUNDED_AGENT_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`, beginning exactly with\n   `# Trellis Urban Heat Continuity Decision` and containing exactly these\n   ordered level-two headings:\n\n   1. `Authority, scope, and operating states`\n   2. `Heat triggers and geographic staging`\n   3. `Power, water, and cooling continuity`\n   4. `Clinical, shelter, and accessibility operations`\n   5. `Transit, communications, logistics, and staffing`\n   6. `Execution, rollback, verification, and closure`\n\nThe final decision must contain 1,200–1,650 words excluding bracketed source\ncitations and cite at least ten distinct exact source IDs. Reconcile authority,\nhazard thresholds, power, water, clinical surge, cooling-center capacity,\naccessible transit, public communication, logistics, staffing, candidate\nlineage, and independent readiness.\n\nBind each action and gate to owners, prerequisites, observations, the current\ncandidate, falsifiers, rollback, and evidence that retires temporary controls.\nPreserve observations versus gates, probability versus coverage, installed\nversus usable capacity, reserve versus flow, median versus percentile, hours\nversus days, source-local authority, and current versus stale evidence.\n\nChecks are candidate-bound mechanical feedback. They do not independently\nauthorize operations, readiness, submission, or closure.\n\n\nEXACT NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULTS\n--- NEWLY EXTERNALIZED RESULT-005 ---\n{\"object_id\":\"batch:CLINIC:1-60+SHELTER:1-60\",\"object_version\":\"9fda639ce00a74b5bbae88dbb9e8f1660587195fbdda7325f3a8942a3894cf77\",\"result_id\":\"RESULT-005\",\"result_kind\":\"source_observation\",\"schema\":\"ceiba-action-result-v1\"}\n--- exact result body ---\n{\"schema\":\"architecture-batch-observation-v0\",\"segments\":[{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"CLINIC\",\"start_line\":1},{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"SHELTER\",\"start_line\":1}],\"total_source_bytes\":8103}\n--- exact batch segment 1 ---\n{\"end_line\":60,\"source_id\":\"CLINIC\",\"source_path\":\"sources/CLINIC_SURGE.md\",\"source_sha256\":\"f8db85fe7f667c38151156fa2c5c25f3601462976e555f637ccff746c13a34b4\",\"source_size_bytes\":5990,\"start_line\":1}\n--- exact source range ---\n# Clinical surge, triage, and ambulance readiness\n\n## Frozen findings\n\nCurrent heat-capable bed occupancy is 71 percent. The surge gate is no more than 82 percent for two consecutive reporting windows and at least twelve staffed cooling beds; occupancy alone is insufficient.\nAmbulance response is 9.8 minutes at p95 against a twelve-minute ceiling. The p95 observation is not a population average or readiness percentage.\nA bed closure, staffing change, triage protocol, ambulance roster, reporting method, or candidate facility change makes prior clinical evidence stale.\n\n## Governing relationships\n\nLABOR supplies licensed coverage, GRID and WATER constrain facilities, and TRANSIT supplies accessible transport alternatives.\nCOUNCIL authorizes public states while REVIEW independently reconciles current clinical blockers.\n\n## Operational evidence\n\n| record | asset/zone | version | measure | unit | status |\n|---|---|---|---:|---|---|\n| CLN-000 | hospital-a | v3 | 71.0 | percent-occupied | superseded |\n| CLN-001 | hospital-b | v3 | 72.7 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-002 | urgent-care | v3 | 71.5 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-003 | ambulance-post | v3 | 73.2 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-004 | hospital-a | v3 | 72.0 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-005 | hospital-b | v3 | 73.7 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-006 | urgent-care | v3 | 72.5 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-007 | ambulance-post | v3 | 71.3 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-008 | hospital-a | v3 | 73.0 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-009 | hospital-b | v3 | 71.8 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-010 | urgent-care | v3 | 73.5 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-011 | ambulance-post | v3 | 72.3 | percent-occupied | current |\n| CLN-012 | ho